---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { companyPolicies, policySourceIndex } from "../../data/policies";
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const linked=companyPolicies.filter(p=>p.link);
const empty=companyPolicies.find(p=>!p.link);
---
<BaseLayout title="Company policies & Group Policy" description="Explore seven documented Windows Group Policy objects, their actual OU links, configured settings and historical tests." breadcrumbs={[{label:"Map",href:"map/"},{label:"Workstation rules"}]}>
<section class="page-head"><div class="container">
<div class="eyebrow">Identity / Group Policy</div>
<h1>IT sets a rule. How do we know it reached the right person?</h1>
<p class="lead" style="margin-top:18px">Nova Corp uses Windows Group Policy to centrally configure passwords, workstations, user desktops and mapped drives. Follow the path from policy to linked directory location—and see where actual client tests exist.</p>
<div class="button-row" style="margin-top:24px">
<a class="btn" href={base+"policies/contractor-usb/"}>Follow the contractor restriction →</a>
<a class="btn ghost" href={base+"directory/"}>Open the directory</a>
</div>
</div></section>
<section class="section compact"><div class="container">
<div class="stats-strip" style="margin-bottom:32px">
<div class="stat"><b>{companyPolicies.length}</b><span>Documented policy objects</span></div>
<div class="stat"><b>{linked.length}</b><span>Enabled, non-enforced links</span></div>
<div class="stat"><b>1</b><span>Created, but empty and unlinked</span></div>
</div>
<div class="paper panel" style="margin-bottom:30px">
 <p class="kicker">Three different questions</p>
 <div class="proof-grid">
  <div><strong>1. Configured</strong><p>What setting is saved inside the policy object?</p></div>
  <div><strong>2. Linked</strong><p>Which domain or OU is assigned the policy, and can its scope include a user or computer?</p></div>
  <div><strong>3. Actually processed/tested</strong><p>Did a real account or workstation process the policy? Was the intended behavior observed?</p></div>
 </div>
 <p class="muted" style="margin-top:18px">An enabled link is not proof of successful application. An applied-policy entry in <code>gpresult</code> does not automatically prove a physical USB device was denied.</p>
</div>
<div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Browse the working setup</div><h2>Policies assigned to the company</h2></div><a class="text-link" href={policySourceIndex}>Source records ↗</a></div>
<div class="card-list">
 {linked.map(p=><a class="system-card" href={base+"policies/"+p.slug+"/"}>
  <small>{p.side} settings · Link enabled, not enforced</small>
  <h3>{p.name}</h3><p>{p.summary}</p>
  <p class="tag-line"><span class="mini-badge">Linked to {p.link?.label}</span></p>
  <span class="readmore">See settings and proof →</span>
 </a>)}
</div>
{empty&&<div class="paper panel" style="margin-top:28px">
 <p class="kicker">Recorded but not deployed</p>
 <h3 style="margin:11px 0">{empty.name}</h3>
 <p class="muted">The keyboard-named Group Policy exists, but has no linked OU and no configured settings. Keyboard preferences were found instead in the Domain Controllers policy.</p>
 <a class="evidence-link" href={base+"policies/"+empty.slug+"/"}>See why it doesn't apply →</a>
</div>}
<div class="note" style="margin-top:26px">All seven GPOs were exported in the documented source review, and each has <strong>Authenticated Users</strong> with Apply Group Policy permission. The effective target still depends on link, inheritance, filtering and processing.</div>
</div></section>
</BaseLayout>
